        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "2fc54698-2ec9-5a46-b80f-de859bc0b193",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Teams: Texas Longhorns, Iowa State Cyclones, Kansas State Wildcats, Baylor Bears\n- People: Mack Brown\n- Places: Darrell K Royal–Texas Memorial Stadium, Manhattan, Kansas\n- Organizations: ESPN\n- Events: 2011 college football season, conference play, Farmageddon series\n\nFacts:\n- In 2011, the Texas Longhorns football team was led by head coach Mack Brown in his 14th year and played home games at Darrell K Royal–Texas Memorial Stadium.\n- In 2011, the Iowa State Cyclones began conference play with a home loss to the Texas Longhorns and finished conference play with a loss at Manhattan, Kansas to the Kansas State Wildcats in the Farmageddon series, ending with a 3–6 conference record.\n- In 2011, the Kansas State Wildcats won three non-conference games against Eastern Kentucky, Kent State, and Miami before opening conference play with a home win over the Baylor Bears.\n- In 2011, the Kansas State Wildcats ended their conference schedule with a victory over rival Iowa State in the Farmageddon showdown.\n- Mack Brown is currently a college football commentator for ESPN.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "6895fac0-13dd-57cb-94b5-dbce49c7433b",
        "text": "Page: 2011 Texas Longhorns football team. Sentence: The Longhorns were led by 14th year head coach Mack Brown and played their home games at Darrell K Royal–Texas Memorial Stadium.\nPage: Mack Brown. Sentence: He is currently a college football commentator for ESPN.\nPage: 2011 Iowa State Cyclones football team. Sentence: The conference play began with a loss at home to the Texas Longhorns, and ended with a loss at Manhattan, Kansas to the Kansas State Wildcats in the Farmageddon series, with a 3–6 record.\nPage: 2011 Kansas State Wildcats football team. Sentence: After winning all three non-conference games (Eastern Kentucky, Kent State, Miami), the conference schedule began with a close victory at home over the Baylor Bears, and ended with a victory over the rival Iowa State Cyclones in the Farmageddon showdown.",
